    "final_message": "The red acceptance test for the story-drafting user story has been successfully written and committed.\n\n**Test Location:** `<repo>/story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`\n\n**Test Name:** `TestSubmitJtbd.test_submitted_jtbd_status_is_drafting`\n\n**What the test does:**\n1. Submits a JTBD (job-to-be-done) with status \"waiting_for_pick\" to the HTTP host\n2. Retrieves the JTBD's status immediately by ID\n3. Asserts that the status is \"drafting\"\n\n**The red failure (expected):**\n```\nAssertionError: assert 'waiting_for_pick' == 'drafting'\n```\n\nThe test correctly fails at the user story's \"then\" requirement: when a JTBD is newly submitted and status is checked immediately, it should be \"drafting\". The generated code currently just echoes back whatever status was submitted, rather than always initializing new JTBDs with \"drafting\" status.\n\n**Verification results:**\n- \u2713 tessercheck passes with zero findings\n- \u2713 mypy --strict passes\n- \u2713 All non-root tests pass (56 passed)\n- \u2713 HTTP host serves successfully\n- \u2713 Restate endpoint registered\n- \u2713 Acceptance test fails at the user story requirement\n\nThe generated tree contains the complete structure for a durable-execution workflow: client, service, orchestrator, action, repository, and HTTP host. Committed at commit `ff8031b`."
